<title>TURKEY: HORSE RACING-TURK GROOMS STOP STRIKE FOR HORSES' SAKE.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-TURK GROOMS STOP STRIKE FOR HORSES' SAKE.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's racehorse grooms have suspended strike action out of concern for the horses.</p>
<p>&quot;They love the horses more than children. They're with the horses from six in the morning till 10 at night; they need a lot of looking after,&quot; grooms' union official Huseyin Meral said.</p>
<p>The grooms, unhappy at earnings of only about $140 a month, agreed to return to work at the weekend ahead of negotiations on Thursday.</p>
